---
title: "authenticated_request_flow (Legion Backend Authentication)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_method: method = request.method
    q_check_method --> q_post_path: method == POST
    q_check_method --> q_get_path: method == GET
    q_post_path --> q_post_sign: signing_string = raw_request_body
    q_get_path --> q_get_sign: signing_string = unique_identifier
    q_post_sign --> q_compute: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, signing_string)
    q_get_sign --> q_compute: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, signing_string)
    q_compute --> q_set_headers: set X-Signature and x-api-key headers
    q_set_headers --> q_send: send request to Legion API
    q_send --> q_server_verify: server extracts X-Signature
    q_server_verify --> q_server_recompute: server recomputes HMAC_SHA256(server_key, expected_string)
    q_server_recompute --> q_compare: compare signatures
    q_compare --> q_authorized: signatures match
    q_compare --> q_denied: signatures do not match
    q_authorized --> [*]: process request
    q_denied --> [*]: revert "401 unauthorized"

    note right of q_check_method
        INV-001: POST and GET use different signing strings - mismatch causes silent auth failure
        INV-002: both x-api-key and X-Signature are required on every request
        INV-003: server-side key must match client-side key for verification to succeed
    end note

    note right of q_compare
        INV-004: no documented rate limiting on failed auth attempts
        INV-005: no documented key rotation mechanism
        INV-006: timing-safe comparison required to prevent signature oracle attacks
    end note
